# Evidence artifacts are content-addressed by sha256 in gate-status.json. Pin them as binary
# (no EOL conversion) so their recorded hashes stay valid on every platform, regardless of the
# consumer's core.autocrlf setting. Stored and checked out byte-for-byte.
.gas-snapshot        -text
deployment-evidence.json -text
gate-status.json     -text
evidence/**          -text

# The submission + the 6-file application package are bound by sha256 in review-target.json
# (closure method v10). Pin them -text too so the recorded review-target hashes reproduce
# byte-for-byte on any checkout (LF), independent of core.autocrlf.
submission.json          -text
compatibility-report.json -text
review-target.json       -text
PROPOSAL.md              -text
THREAT_MODEL.md          -text
TEST_PLAN.md             -text
EVIDENCE.md              -text
LICENSE                  -text

# Source and test Solidity are bound by sha256 in review-target.json (closure v10).
# Pin them -text so the recorded hashes reproduce byte-for-byte on every checkout (LF),
# independent of core.autocrlf. Without this, autocrlf smudges an LF-committed blob to
# CRLF in the worktree, so a rebuilt review-target no longer matches the exact HEAD blob.
*.sol -text
